WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.520
Delete a gene in the whole animal, and you learn what a protein does, not what a

2
00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:16.140
cell type does. A deletion from birth is a developmental experiment: the animal can

3
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:18.240
adjust before you test it.

4
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.040
Remove chosen cells instead; ask whether they are needed.

5
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:29.510
Before gene-targeted toxins, a laser could kill one identified cell.

6
00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:33.090
A young larva is held still with azide.

7
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:39.530
Most worm cells sit in reproducible positions, and each type has a typical nucleus

8
00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:44.430
under Nomarski optics, so position plus nucleus names the cell.

9
00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:49.290
The beam is focused on a single spot, aligned with that cell.

10
00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.850
Pulses are brief, so heat has little time to spread to neighbours.

11
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:59.630
In one 1995 system, they lasted three nanoseconds.

12
00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.150
An hour to a day later, the killed nucleus is gone.

13
00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:07.073
A laser needs a see-through animal.

14
00:01:07.853 --> 00:01:13.233
A genetic toxin reaches any cell that carries its receptor, even deep in the brain.

15
00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:19.593
Mouse cells are poor targets for diphtheria toxin; the human receptor binds it with

16
00:01:19.593 --> 00:01:22.393
about 100,000 times higher affinity.

17
00:01:23.353 --> 00:01:28.733
So the human receptor gene goes under a chosen gene's control, or into an allele

18
00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:32.223
where Cre removes a stop cassette blocking the receptor,

19
00:01:32.273 --> 00:01:34.813
so a Cre line chooses the cells.

20
00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:38.423
The toxin is injected when you choose.

21
00:01:39.043 --> 00:01:44.923
For example, 100 micrograms per kilogram, on two days, 72 hours apart.

22
00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:49.483
Inside a sensitive cell, it inhibits protein synthesis.

23
00:01:50.483 --> 00:01:56.163
Because the timing is yours, the same cells can be removed in a newborn or an adult.

24
00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:03.507
Results have two parts: a count of target cells left, and a behaviour compared with

25
00:02:03.507 --> 00:02:10.067
controls. In one study, over 98% of Mrgprd neurons were gone.

26
00:02:10.907 --> 00:02:17.767
The mechanical withdrawal threshold rose from 0.41 grams to 0.99, with no

27
00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:21.067
significant change in wild-type littermates given the toxin.

28
00:02:22.167 --> 00:02:24.427
Heat and cold sensitivity were not reduced.

29
00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:30.987
The toxin might act on animals without the receptor, so give it to wild-type

30
00:02:30.987 --> 00:02:34.827
littermates. Too few cells might die, so count them.

31
00:02:35.807 --> 00:02:41.187
One Cre-driven toxin killed Paneth cells incompletely; a receptor knock-in

32
00:02:41.187 --> 00:02:42.667
removed virtually all.

33
00:02:43.647 --> 00:02:47.687
In one mouse line, the toxin depleted two spleen macrophage types.

34
00:02:48.327 --> 00:02:50.567
Check other cells, and use a second method.

35
00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:59.460
In 1981, Kimble and White used a laser to kill a worm gonad's distal tip cell.

36
00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.060
Germ cells that would divide entered meiosis instead.

37
00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:12.840
In 1987, Austin and Kimble found that glp-1 mutants mimic this, which led to a

38
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:14.000
Notch-like receptor.

39
00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.200
The laser was needed because no gene was yet known.

40
00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:26.533
In 2005, Luquet and colleagues killed AgRP neurons in adult mice, causing rapid

41
00:03:26.533 --> 00:03:32.053
starvation. Killed in newborns, the same neurons had minimal effect on feeding.

42
00:03:32.973 --> 00:03:34.773
Timing exposed compensation.

43
00:03:36.013 --> 00:03:42.953
In 2019, van Es and colleagues removed Paneth cells, yet Lgr5 stem cells persisted.

44
00:03:42.953 --> 00:03:50.213
Keep this rule: removal shows whether cells are needed, for that assay, age and

45
00:03:50.213 --> 00:03:53.133
targeting tool, not what they can do alone.
